592 |  * @c: string to copy
593 |  *
594 |  * cfg_strdup() creates a new copy of the string in the memory
595 |  * pool associated with the configuration being currently parsed.
596 |  * It's often used when a string literal occurs in the configuration
597 |  * and we want to preserve it for further use.
598 |  */
599 | char *
