304 |  * DOC: Memory blocks
305 |  *
306 |  * Memory blocks are pieces of contiguous allocated memory.
307 |  * They are a bit non-standard since they are represented not by a pointer
308 |  * to &resource, but by a void pointer to the start of data of the
309 |  * memory block. All memory block functions know how to locate the header
