 10 | /**
 11 |  * DOC: Route aggregation
 12 |  *
 13 |  * This is an implementation of route aggregation functionality.
 14 |  * It enables user to specify a set of route attributes in the configuarion file
 15 |  * and then, for a given destination (net), aggregate routes with the same
 16 |  * values of these attributes into a single multi-path route.
 17 |  *
 18 |  * Structure &channel contains pointer to aggregation list which is represented
 19 |  * by &aggr_list_linearized. In rt_notify_aggregated(), attributes from this
 20 |  * list are evaluated for every route of a given net and results are stored
 21 |  * in &rte_val_list which contains pointer to this route and array of &f_val.
 22 |  * Array of pointers to &rte_val_list entries is sorted using
 23 |  * sort_rte_val_list(). For comparison of &f_val structures, val_compare()
 24 |  * is used. Comparator function is written so that sorting is stable. If all
 25 |  * attributes have the same values, routes are compared by their global IDs.
 26 |  *
 27 |  * After sorting, &rte_val_list entries containing equivalent routes will be
 28 |  * adjacent to each other. Function process_rte_list() iterates through these
 29 |  * entries to identify sequences of equivalent routes. New route will be
 30 |  * created for each such sequence, even if only from a single route.
 31 |  * Only attributes from the aggreagation list will be set for the new route.
 32 |  * New &rta is created and prepare_rta() is used to copy static and dynamic
 33 |  * attributes to new &rta from &rta of the original route. New route is created
 34 |  * by create_merged_rte() from new &rta and exported to the routing table.
 35 |  */
 36 | 
 37 | #undef LOCAL_DEBUG
