  12 |  * Supported standards:
  13 |  * o RFC 7854 - BMP standard
  14 |  *
  15 |  * TODO:
  16 |  * - Support Peer Distinguisher ID in Per-Peer Header
  17 |  * - Support peer type as RD Instance in Peer Type field of Per-Peer Header.
  18 |  *   Currently, there are supported Global and Local Instance Peer types
  19 |  * - Support corresponding FSM event code during send PEER DOWN NOTIFICATION
  20 |  * - Support DE_CONFIGURED PEER DOWN REASON code in PEER DOWN NOTIFICATION message
  21 |  * - If connection with BMP collector will lost then we don't establish connection again
  22 |  * - Set Peer Type by its a global and local-scope IP address
  23 |  *
  24 |  * The BMP session is managed by a simple state machine with three states: Idle
  25 |  * (!started, !sk), Connect (!started, sk active), and Established (started). It
  26 |  * has three events: connect successful (Connect -> Established), socket error
  27 |  * (any -> Idle), and connect timeout (Idle/Connect -> Connect, resetting the
