1981 | /**
1982 |  * sk_send - send data to a socket
1983 |  * @s: socket
1984 |  * @len: number of bytes to send
1985 |  *
1986 |  * This function sends @len bytes of data prepared in the
1987 |  * transmit buffer of the socket @s to the network connection.
1988 |  * If the packet can be sent immediately, it does so and returns
1989 |  * 1, else it queues the packet for later processing, returns 0
1990 |  * and calls the @tx_hook of the socket when the tranmission
1991 |  * takes place.
1992 |  */
